"""Hand-written conversational seeds for Nik (romanized Nepali).

Each intent = (user phrasings, Nik replies). gen_sft.py samples a phrasing,
applies real-world chat spelling noise (xa / tw / tmro / k / ni ...), and pairs
it with a reply. The model learns intent -> reply *style*, not a lookup: there
are many phrasings per intent, many intents, and replies are mixed with
open-ended writing and reasoning data during training.
"""

